{# One achievement in an e-mail: its badge at 48 px (the PNG at 2x, absolute URL - mail apps load nothing relative)
   and the text, as a row of the caller's table. The picture's alt is empty on purpose: the text beside it names the
   achievement and tier, and a mail app that blocks images, a screen reader and the plain-text part
   (EmailHtmlToTextConverter writes every alt) would otherwise say it twice.
   Params: type (BadgeType), tier (null|BadgeTier), label, detail (null|string) #}
<tr>
    <td width="48" style="width: 48px; padding: 6px 12px 6px 0; vertical-align: middle;">
        <img src="{{ badge_art_url(type, tier, 'png', 96, absolute = true) }}" alt="" width="48" height="48" style="display: block; width: 48px; height: 48px; border: 0;">
    </td>
    <td style="padding: 6px 0; vertical-align: middle;">
        <strong>{{ label }}</strong>{% if detail is not empty %}<br>{{ detail }}{% endif %}
    </td>
</tr>
